  "hints": ["A big bead in front of a smaller one is worth cutting, as long as you may still cut: the row then starts smaller.", "Work out how many beads you may cut: LENGTH MINUS keep. Go through the beads with a NEW STACK: WHILE cuts remain and the bead on top is GREATER THAN the new bead, POP it and use up one cut. Then PUSH the new bead.", "If cuts remain at the end, POP them off the top. The stack now holds the answer with its last bead on top: fill a list of keep places from the back with SET ELEMENT."],
